Tutor's brief for the digital edition (982 pp., native text): 'extrae del
capitulo 2. Desde la pag 258 a la 283 del pdf, extrae los que consideres
mas dificiles o los mas integradores' — Chapter 2 'Ejercicios propuestos',
printed pp. 225-250, answer key pp. 938-939.

40 fixed bilingual templates, every answer double-verified (printed key +
independent sympy; download/verify_espol_ch2.py, 41/41 checks):
- polynomials/factoring 34e 36a 36b 36d 36e + equations 78a
- rational 35l (telescoping) 37a 37b 37d + equations 48 (empty truth set)
- radicals/equations 80b (spurious root) 80e
- linear-equations abs 54d 54e (interval, text type) 54j + literal 78c 78d
- quadratics 49 (Vieta trap) 82 (unique solution) 83 (free fall, g cancels)
  84 (cyclist, numeric-unit)
- systems/applications 47 56 58 60 61 62 63 64c 68 70
- sequences 125 129 136 139 141 146 147 151

Notable:
- #82: printed key lists only k=9/4; the complete answer is k in {0, 9/4}
  (k=0 makes it linear with a unique solution) — shipped verified, flagged.
- #77a dropped: it duplicates quad-espol-112 (3.11-112a, scanned edition) —
  same equation 4x^2-4xy-y^2=1.
- #151 has no printed key — sympy-only (128 terms, 105..994, sum 70336).
- Drive-by fix: rad-espol-128b/128c now shuffle their MC options (they
  shipped with the correct option always first).
- Bank: 603 -> 643 templates; validate:content 0 errors / 0 warnings;
  tsc + eslint clean; agent-browser QA across all five answer formats,
  ES/EN, mobile 390px, dark mode.
